import mundane theorem    stdlib/numbers/square-nonneg

theorem negative-quadratic
  note        If x were at least 0, then x² and 5x would both be at least
              0, and so would their sum.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  assume x² + 5x < 0                                                  (H2)
  then x < 0

1.  x < 0
    contradiction
    suppose not x < 0                                                 (S)

    1.1.  x ≥ 0
          inequalities, from S

    1.2.  x² ≥ 0
          mun:square-nonneg

    1.3.  5·x ≥ 0
          inequalities
            x ≥ 0           1.1
            5·x ≥ 0         multiplying by 5

    1.4.  x² + 5x ≥ 0
          inequalities, from 1.2, 1.3

    1.5.  not x² + 5x < 0
          inequalities, from 1.4, contradicting H2
